# rct sessions: one `claude remote-control` server per line, each in its own
# tmux window named after the session. Edit with `rct edit`, then `rct up`
# (new lines) or `rct restart <name>` (changed lines).
#
#   <name>   <folder>   [options]
#
# name     tmux window name and the session title at claude.ai/code. Keep it short,
#          no spaces. `rct a <name>` jumps straight to it.
# folder   where the server runs. ~ is fine. Avoid ~ itself: Claude Code never saves
#          trust for the home folder, so it would ask on every start.
# options  chrome=on|off       let sessions use Claude in Chrome on this machine
#          mode=<mode>         starting permission mode: default, acceptEdits, plan, auto
#          spawn=same-dir|worktree   worktree gives each new session its own git worktree.
#                              In a git folder with no spawn=, rct uses same-dir.
#          capacity=<N>        max concurrent sessions (default 32)
#          model=<model>       model for the sessions: opus, sonnet, or a full model id
#          effort=<level>      PIN effort (low, medium, high, xhigh, max). For a default you can
#                              still change from the app, set "effortLevel" in ~/.claude/settings.json
#          host=<glob>         only start on matching machines (`hostname -s`), so one
#                              file can be shared between this Mac and the headless box
#          --any-flag          passed straight to `claude remote-control`
#
# A `default` line sets options for every line below it. Several `default` lines
# add up, and a later value for the same key wins. `default clear` starts over.

default chrome=on model=opus

# --- Personal -------------------------------------------------------------
dev          ~/Development
blog         ~/Development/blog

# --- Work (kept separate from personal) -----------------------------------
work         ~/Development/work
work-api     ~/Development/work/api

# --- Headless box: no one watching, so no Chrome unless asked -------------
# default chrome=off host=mini*
# mini-dev     ~/Development
